    "title": "Download from an IP literal into a temp dir",
    "desc": "A program ran curl/wget against a bare IP address (not a hostname) writing into /tmp, /dev/shm or /var/tmp. Fetching a payload by IP into a scratch dir is a classic first stage: it skips DNS and any name allow-list, and legitimate automation almost always fetches from a named host. The attempt is the signal whether or not the fetch succeeds.",
